<article class="env-remark" id="4FF0C2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4FF0C2">Remark <span data-tag="4FF0C2">3.2.2.2</span>.</a> More generally, let $f: [m] \rightarrow [n]$ be an order-preserving map, inducing a map $\Delta ^ m \rightarrow \Delta ^ n$. Then $M(\phi ) \times _{\Delta ^ n} \Delta ^ m$ is naturally isomorphic to $M(\phi ')$, where the sequence $\phi '$ is given by </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A^{f(0)} \leftarrow \ldots \leftarrow A^{f(m)}. \]
</div>
</article>